.*
.* WRKSBS: the active subsystems, their storage and the system pools
.* their subsystem pools are.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SBSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 12'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STGCL BASETYPE='ZONED 9 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=POOLCL BASETYPE='ZONED 1 0'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=SBS CLASS=SBSCL.
:VAR NAME=SBSLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STORAGE CLASS=STGCL.
:VAR NAME=P1 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P2 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P3 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P4 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P5 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P6 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P7 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P8 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P9 CLASS=POOLCL.
:VAR NAME=P10 CLASS=POOLCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=SBS VARS='OPT SBS SBSLIB STORAGE P1 P2 P3 P4 P5 P6 P7 P8 P9 P10'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/SBSKEYS' NAME=SBSKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display system data
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F14 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSSTS'.F14=Work with system status
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSBS KEYL=SBSKEYS HELP=WRKSBS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with Subsystems
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=SBS.(No subsystems are active)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD ?ENDSBS SBS(&SBS.)'.4=End subsystem
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPSBSD SBSD(&SBSLIB./&SBS.)'.5=Display subsystem description
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSBS/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKSBSJOB SBS(&SBS.)'.8=Work with subsystem jobs
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKSBS/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/SBS' VAR=SBS USAGE=OUTPUT.Subsystem
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/STORAGE' VAR=STORAGE USAGE=OUTPUT.Total Storage (M)
:LISTGRP.-----------Subsystem Pools------------
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P1' VAR=P1 USAGE=OUTPUT.1
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P2' VAR=P2 USAGE=OUTPUT.2
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P3' VAR=P3 USAGE=OUTPUT.3
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P4' VAR=P4 USAGE=OUTPUT.4
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P5' VAR=P5 USAGE=OUTPUT.5
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P6' VAR=P6 USAGE=OUTPUT.6
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P7' VAR=P7 USAGE=OUTPUT.7
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P8' VAR=P8 USAGE=OUTPUT.8
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P9' VAR=P9 USAGE=OUTPUT.9
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/P10' VAR=P10 USAGE=OUTPUT.10
:ELISTGRP.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKSBS.Work with Subsystems - Help
:P.Every active subsystem with the main storage its pools hold and,
under each subsystem pool number, the system pool it is. Type an
option next to a subsystem, or a command on the command line.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SBSKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F11=Display system data
:PD.Display system data.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F14=Work with system status
:PD.Runs WRKSYSSTS.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSBS/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBS'.Subsystem
:P.The subsystem of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STORAGE'.Total Storage (M)
:P.The total Storage (M) of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P1'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 1
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 1 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P2'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 2
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 2 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P3'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 3
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 3 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P4'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 4
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 4 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P5'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 5
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 5 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P6'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 6
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 6 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P7'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 7
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 7 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P8'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 8
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 8 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P9'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 9
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 9 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/P10'.-----------Subsystem Pools------------ 10
:P.The -----------Subsystem Pools------------ 10 of each entry in the
list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSBS/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.4=End subsystem
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end subsystem it. The End
Subsystem (ENDSBS) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Display subsystem description
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display subsystem
description it. The Display Subsystem Description (DSPSBSD) command runs
for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with subsystem jobs
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with subsystem jobs
it. The Work with Subsystem Jobs (WRKSBSJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
